+	/*
+	 * k13d: before blaming the INIT message, find out whether the firmware is still alive at all without it.
+	 * sweetwmiidle=<seconds> sits still after the service-ready events, polling the event rings; if SYS_ERR
+	 * arrives anyway the crash has nothing to do with INIT and we are missing something the firmware needs
